--- body ---
## Context

Docs visit, 2026-10-29 (`memory/journal/2026/2026-10-29-docs-visit-first-global.md`,
finding B), ticketed at the author's request the same day.

`rules/workflow.md` § Session start says "Enter the worktree before answering
(exceptions and naming: `claude-code.md`)". The naming table, the `/hunt N`
exception (do not create a worktree before the skill runs: its detached agent
creates its own) and the self-presentation line live in `rules/claude-code.md`
§ Entering the session. The Pi and Codex adapters skip `rules/claude-code.md`
(`rules/README.md`, adapter projections), so on those runtimes the session-start
rule points at text they never load. Consequence: a Pi or Codex session can create
a worktree before `/hunt N` and orphan it, and names worktrees without the table.
Molt reclaims orphans, so nothing corrupts; the cost is clutter and a rule that
does not hold on two first-class runtimes. The self-presentation line is also
stated twice (`workflow.md` and `claude-code.md`).

Unverified on a live Pi or Codex session: confirm the adapters' load set before
editing.

## Intent

Move what every runtime needs into `rules/workflow.md`: the worktree naming table,
the `/hunt N` exception, the plain-git recipe pointer (`skills/hunt/SKILL.md`
§ Worktree) and the one self-presentation line. `rules/claude-code.md` keeps only
what is true of Claude Code alone (never call `EnterWorktree`, and why) and points
to workflow.md for the rest. One home per fact; no restatement.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The Pi and Codex adapters' load sets are checked, and the PR states which rule files each loads
- [ ] `rules/workflow.md` holds the naming table, the `/hunt N` exception and the self-presentation line; `rules/claude-code.md` keeps only the Claude Code specifics and a pointer
- [ ] The self-presentation line is stated once
- [ ] Every reference to the moved text (grep `claude-code.md` across rules/, skills/, hooks/, adapters/) points at its new home
- [ ] The harness gate passes

Priced in the visit: about 15 resident lines moved, about 30 agent-minutes and
5 author-minutes, odds 0.8 that it removes the orphan path. Resident rules: the
author reviews the wording.
